ing ray tracing to the game after  launch but did not mention if ray  tracing will be featured in both the pc  and console editions  but the trailers don't stop there dice  also dropped a new video that revealed  the final five specialist characters  that will be featured in battlefield  2042 at launch specialist characters  represent a big change for the  battlefield series which has in the past  relied on more rigid class types but not  distinct characters like in 2042 these  new specialists include navin rayo a  recon soldier whose trojan network trait  reveals enemies around them after  killing a hacked target santiago  espinosa an assault character that  wields a ballistic shield and can  survive blasts better than others emma  rozier another assault character who can  fly with the wingsuit and has a variety  of smart explosives jisoo pake who is a  recon soldier who can detect nearby  enemies and use a scanner to reveal the  location of hostiles and cover and  constantine angel a support character  who can heal teammates faster than  normal and drop a crate that lets  players switch loadouts and also  contains armor and ammo for teammates  and speaking of new things coming to  your favorite shooters respawn announced  a new apex legends map a new trailer for  the game's upcoming season escape shows  off beaches jungles and strange features  of what looked to be an upcoming vr map  along with ash the newest legend the  trailer kicks off with the game's cast  relaxing on the beach which only lasts  for so long before monstrous wildlife  begins attacking the spiders from the  trailer hint that we're on planet gaia  but it's not clear what role these  monsters will play when the map actually  launches or if they'll interact with the  players at all it's possible that the  monsters will simply be window dressing  for the map that being said a page on ea  site going over the event says quote no  matter how beautiful it seems every  corner of outlands is a dangerous 